    {
      "ordinal": 24,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "5.3",
      "title": "Specific Requirements",
      "body": "The suspension system consists of vervelles, a piece of leather, and thread.\n\n● Vervelles: These are metal components with a hole, allowing threads (metal or leather) to pass through.\n● Leather Piece: The aventail (chainmail neck guard) is attached to a leather piece, which can be riveted or sewn.\n● Thread: The thread, made of either metal or leather (or materials that replicate their look), passes through the vervelles to secure the leather piece to the helmet.\n\nAlternative Method for fabric aventail: the aventail can be sewn directly to the helmet’s edge.",
